# DRY and SOLID Principles

## Communication and Problem-Solving

- If clarification is needed on any part of the task, ask before implementing.
- When outputting code blocks, include a file name comment before the block with a few lines of surrounding context so the user can locate changes.

## Code Quality and Best Practices

- Follow DRY: do not duplicate logic — extract shared behavior into reusable functions, classes, or modules.
- Apply SOLID principles, especially Single Responsibility and Dependency Inversion, when structuring features.

## Paradigms and Principles

- Stick to the current architecture choices (see `pubspec.yaml` and existing project structure) unless the user suggests a new approach.
- Prefer semantic naming and abstractions that reflect domain concepts, not implementation details.
- Think in terms of platform constraints (Flutter mobile/web/desktop) when designing solutions.

## Handling Uncertainty

- Do not guess at requirements or architecture decisions.
- Surface trade-offs when multiple valid approaches exist.
